    <body>
      <div xml:id="gom-prov15">
        <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e98">Caput 15</head>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e100">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e102">Versus 1</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e104">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e106" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_1@1-4">Responsio mollis frangit iram.</quote>
            Qui verba increpantis humiliter suscipit, jam propinquat veniae reatus quem gessit. Qui arguenti resultat, contra se iram judicis provocat.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e111">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e113">Versus 2</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e115">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e117" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_2@7-8">Ebullit stultitiam.</quote>
            Scripturam pervertendo, suos sensus auctoritati praeponendo; velut fatui philosophi, ut Porphyrius, et Julianus, qui contra <pb ed="#P" n="1098A"/> Ecclesiae doctores stultitiae suae fluenta fundebant.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e124">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e126">Versus 5</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e128">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e130" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_5@1-2">Stultus irridet.</quote>
            Stultus est omnis peccator, qui, terrenis actibus deditus, futurum nihil praevidet: is disciplinam irridet, dum derogat divinae correctioni.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e135">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e137">Versus 7</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e139">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e141" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_7@5-7">Cor stultorum dissimile.</quote>
            Vel dissimile sibi ipsi, variis cogitationibus, et nunquam idem manet. Contra quod de Anna dicitur: <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e144" source="http://scta.info/resource/Isam1_18@20-27">Vultusque ejus non sunt amplius in diversa mutati.</quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e150">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e152">Versus 10</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e154">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e156" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_10">Doctrina mala. Qui solverit unum de mandatis istis minimis, et docuerit sic homines, minimus est in regno coelorum.</quote>
            <!-- check: lemma not matched to verse text -->
            Talibus tamen, si correcti fuerint, patet reditus ad veniam: si autem increpationes non receperint, omnino morientur.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e163">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e165">Versus 15</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e167">
            <pb ed="#P" n="1098B"/>
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e171" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_15@1-2">Omnes dies.</quote>
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e174"><seg type="qs">Omne tempus populi Dei</seg>, etc., usque ad <seg type="qs">quasi jugi delectantur convivio.</seg></quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e183">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e185">Versus 17</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e187">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e189" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_17@1-5">Melius est vocari ad olera.</quote>
            Multo enim utilius est simplicis vitae innocentiam cum charitate servare, etc., <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e192" source="http://scta.info/resource/lc13_27@8-13">usque ad, discedite a me operarii iniquitatis.</quote>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e197">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e199">Versus 19</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e201">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e203" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_19@2-2">Pigrorum,</quote>
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e206"><seg type="qs">quos piget operari justitiam</seg>, etc., usque ad <seg type="qs">sed quia hoc bonos non praepedit, adjungit:</seg></quote>
          </p>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e214">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e216" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_19@6-9">Via justorum absque offendiculo.</quote>
            Justi enim quidquid adversitatis in sua conversatione invenerint, non offendunt, quia aeternae spei et internae contemplationis saltu adversa transiliunt.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e221">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e223">Versus 23</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e225">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e227" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_23@1-2">Laetatur homo.</quote>
            Humanum est de <pb ed="#P" n="1098C"/> sententia quasi prudenter prolata laetari. Sed vere sapiens non solum quod loquitur, sed etiam opportunitatem loci, et temporis, et personae cui loquitur, diligenter inquirit.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e234">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e236">Versus 24</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e238">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e240" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_24@7-9">De inferno novissimo,</quote>
            etc. Primus infernus caecitas peccantis animae, et verae lucis scientia carentis, de quo: <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e243" source="http://scta.info/resource/ps54_16@6-9">Descendunt in infernum viventes</quote>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e249">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e251">Versus 25</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e253">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e255" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_25">Viduae Ecclesiae,</quote>
            <!-- check: lemma not matched to verse text -->
            scilicet sponsae suae, pro cujus vita mori dignatus est.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e262">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e264">Versus 26</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e266">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e268" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_26">Firmabitur:</quote>
            <!-- check: lemma not matched to verse text -->
            in judicio, quando non solum factis, sed et verbis omnibus digna praemia reddet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div xml:id="gom-prov15-Dd1e275">
          <head xml:id="gom-prov15-Hd1e277">Versus 30</head>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e279">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e281" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_30@1-4">Lux oculorum laetificat animam.</quote>
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e284"><seg type="qs">Jure mentem delectat humanam</seg>, etc., usque ad <seg type="qs">sic enim <pb ed="#P" n="1098D"/> magis fervet opus.</seg></quote>
          </p>
          <p xml:id="gom-prov15-d1e294">
            <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e296" type="lemma" source="http://scta.info/resource/prov15_30@1-2">Lux oculorum.</quote>
            Alia translatio: <quote xml:id="gom-prov15-Qd1e299">Videns bona oculus delectat corda bona,</quote> scilicet, Domini in terra viventium, quae, quia in oculo mentis contemplatur, merito corde delectatur, quamvis affligatur exterius.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </body>
